488						"engine reached through DOCKER_HOST or a remote context is not detected as remote: " +
489						"it can show another machine's network, and the trace still leaves from this machine.\n\n" +
490						"The bridge row appears only when this machine has the interface of the container's " +
491						"network bridge, read on this machine; otherwise no bridge is shown. A remote engine " +
492						"whose network is also called docker0 can match this machine's interface by name.\n\n" +
493						"When the container's bridge is not on this machine, the engine row reads " +
494						"internal path not visible (location unknown): the engine may run in a VM, remote " +
495						"or rootless, and DevDesk does not guess. When it cannot check, the row reads " +
496						"undetermined (bridge not verified). The hops are traced from this machine (the " +
497						"host, or the WSL VM when DevDesk runs under WSL); DevDesk cannot see inside the " +
498						"engine's VM.",
499				},
500				{
501					Title: "Interfaces Tab — How it works",
502					Body: "Lists this machine's network interfaces, read in this process — no container, " +
503						"no Docker. Name, state, MTU, hardware address, error counters and every address " +
504						"the interface carries. ctrl+r re-reads them.\n\n" +
505						"A dash is not a zero. RX err and TX err show a dash when the counters could not " +
506						"be read at all, which is a different thing from an interface that has dropped " +
507						"nothing; MTU shows one where the platform reports no figure, as Windows does " +
508						"for its loopback.\n\n" +
509						"This was the Topology tab. Its routing table, ARP cache and firewall summary " +
510						"were read by running ip and iptables in a container on the Docker Desktop VM, " +
511						"so they described the VM and not this machine. Nothing portable produces them, " +
512						"so they were removed rather than translated — and the route question moved to " +
513						"the Diagnostics tab, where it is asked about a target: the Local route check " +
514						"names the interface your traffic to that host actually leaves by.",
515				},
516				{
517					Title: "Where the checks run",
518					Body: "Everything here runs in this process, on this machine's network stack: the " +
519						"diagnostic checks, the socket table, the interfaces and the path trace alike. They answer for " +
520						"the resolver, the routing table, the sockets and the VPN you are actually on, " +
521						"and nothing needs Docker.\n\n" +
522						"The route trace used to be the exception. It ran traceroute in a container " +
523						"started with --network host, which on Docker Desktop is the Linux VM's " +
524						"namespace — so it traced the path from the VM and not from here, and the two " +
525						"are not the same network. It was removed rather than kept with a caveat.\n\n" +
526						"The trace is back, in this process: the Path tab sends its own probes from this " +
527						"machine's network stack, so it answers for the network you are actually on. The " +
528						"Local route check still names the interface and source address your traffic to a " +
529						"target leaves by — the split-tunnel answer, read from this machine.",
530				},
531			},
532		}
533	}
